This folder contains the R code and data files accompanying the manuscript 

"Prediction intervals for random-effects meta-analysis based on confidence 
distributions and Edgington's method"

by David Kronthaler and Leonhard Held.

Files

* code_manuscript.R: R script to reproduce the analyses presented in the manuscript.
* code_supplementary_material.R: R script to reproduce the analyses presented in the 
  Supplementary Material. This script also generates the files timeCDEdgington.RDS 
  and MCvsGAQ.RDS.
* functions/utility_functions.R: Utility functions used by both R scripts.
* data/Covid_example.Rdata: Data for the COVID example.
* data/Serenoa_example.Rdata: Data for the Serenoa example.
* data/timeCDEdgington.RDS: Results for the computation time analysis of the CD-Edgington 
  method.
* data/MCvsGAQ.RDS: Results comparing the Monte Carlo and GAQ implementations of the 
  CD-Edgington method.
* ../results/: Folder containing 120 .RDS files, one for each simulation scenario 
  considered in the simulation study.

To run the code

Install the required R packages listed in the library() calls at the beginning of 
the corresponding R script. Set the working directory to this folder and run either
code_manuscript.R or code_supplementary_material.R. The directory structure should
be preserved.